    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nWhen an owner is created without a `registrationDate`, the server now defaults it to the current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format. A supplied date is preserved.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` is defined as `allOf` including `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both accepted on create and returned on read. `format: date` generates a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 After mapping the request, if no registration date was supplied it defaults to `LocalDate.now()`. MapStruct handles the DTO\u2194entity mapping automatically by name.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change was required there; the others were updated for consistency.",
